WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.870
Good morning Hank it's Monday. First I have
to correct something about your video from

00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:07.050
Friday: You said the Project For Awesome begins
at midnight on December 17th, in fact it begins

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:13.130
at Noon Eastern time December 17th. So upload
your videos as close to noon as possible and

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:14.130
then tune into youtube.com/p4a.

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:15.709
So Hank today I want to tell you about 8 things
I love.

00:00:15.709 --> 00:00:21.619
Thing one: this book, 'Anna and the French
Kiss' by Stephanie Perkins. Holy Snood do

00:00:21.619 --> 00:00:25.130
I love this book! So a couple years ago at
LeakyCon a Nerdfighter comes up to me and

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:28.470
she says: "I'm a Nerdfighter and I wrote a
book, it's coming out in 2010, can I send

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:31.939
you a copy?" and I said, "sure". Right so
flash forward 2 years, I get this book in

00:00:31.939 --> 00:00:34.280
the mail and I'm like "I'll read a page or
two," and then I can't stop reading it because

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:38.380
it is made of sweetness and funny and awesome.
Hank, 'Anna and the French Kiss' is like Maureen

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:45.649
Johnson and I had a baby, a French baby. No,
it is nothing like that. But it is super-funny

00:00:45.649 --> 00:00:49.309
and smart and one of the most genuinely romantic
stories I have ever read.

00:00:49.309 --> 00:00:53.829
Second thing I love: Karen Kavett, who designed
that. Karen has been a Nerdighter forever,

00:00:53.829 --> 00:00:57.260
she designed the Project for Awesome thumbnail
this year, she did all the French Revolution

00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:59.769
videos, and I'm just so grateful for her.

00:00:59.769 --> 00:01:03.760
Thing three: Beckoning Lovely. Hank, as you
know I'm obsessed with my friend Amy Krouse

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:08.070
Rosenthal's Beckoning of Lovely project, in
which she tries to beckon lovely things into

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:12.720
the world. You can find a link to what happened
on 10/10/10 in Chicago in the dooblydoo, and

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:17.400
it might make you cry. It makes me cry, uhh,
but I'm a crier. Hank I don't think you've

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:21.210
ever cried in any of our videos, I'd like
to see you cry in a video. I can't-I don't

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:25.400
think I've seen you cry since you were a kid.
Probably the last time I saw you cry was when

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:26.420
I was punching you.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:31.560
Thing four: this shirt, which is currently
stuck on my glasses, and which was given to

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:33.399
me by Nerimon. Thanks Alex!

00:01:33.399 --> 00:01:37.680
Thing five: Charlie. So Hank I met Charlie
McDonnell when he was, to use the language

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:41.700
of his native country, but a young lad. But
even back then I remember thinking, "This

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:46.700
kid, aside from being outrageously handsome,
is kind of a genius." Ever since, Charlie

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:51.229
has been proving me right, but never more
than on his new album 'This is Me', which

00:01:51.229 --> 00:01:55.780
is honestly-I haven't been able to stop listening
to it on iTunes. It's the only thing in my

00:01:55.780 --> 00:02:05.149
iTunes. I have 'Bread' on repeat, and I've
listened to it..621 times. This raises the

00:02:05.149 --> 00:02:09.750
alarming possibility that I might technically
be a fangirl. Also, on the back of his CD

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:14.470
he wrote, "I hope you like it" and then "Hopeful
Charlie". I liked it, Charlie.

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:17.800
Thing six: white dog on white snow.

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:21.640
Thing seven: Hank, I have perhaps saved the
best for nearly last. So a couple weeks ago

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:25.320
my friend Joe Felice asked me to participate
in 'The Station is Watching You', a show that

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:30.580
works to give new YouTubers a bigger audience.
Joe chose for me a user named Vi Hart, and

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:35.030
French the Llama is she amazing! The crazy
part of the story is that Vi Hart has been

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:41.670
a Nerdfighter since 2007 and in fact designed
the original Nerdfighter pirate logo. Nerdfighters-

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:48.290
click here, watch a Vi Hart video, and your
whole life will be changed. You may think

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:52.321
you hate Math, but you don't hate Math, you
hate the way you've been taught Math. Hank

00:02:52.321 --> 00:02:56.670
she can also play Jingle Bells with candy
buttons, which is a major development in the

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:58.400
history of candy buttons.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:03.200
And lastly Hank, thing eight: the Napoleon.
So Hank this is Napoleon, and lately my son

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:07.190
Henry has taken to pointing in the direction
he would like to be taken. Hank, I love the

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:12.300
Napoleon because Henry clearly believes that
I am a horse. He's like: "And now we shall

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:15.280
head that way, horse. To the candy!"

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:19.790
So Hank that's stuff I love: Nerdfighters
writing books and making music and making

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:24.370
videos about mathemusicianship. Nerdfighters,
please tell me some stuff that you love so

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:45.910
I can find new stuff to love, and Hank - don't
forget to be awesome.

